  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AJOL core support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African Journals Online (AJOL) is a non-profit organization working for increased quality, quantity, accessibility, recognition, and use of African-published research. AJOL is an online publishing platform &#x2013; based on Free and Open-Source software &#x2013; of peer-reviewed, African research journals in all research disciplines and in several African languages. AJOL provides quality assessment of and support to hundreds of research journals throughout the African continent, journal-specific mentoring, online training and webinars, online hosting of journals and Open Access resources. It also promotes the voice and representation of African academic publishing in global forums.

AJOL&#x2019;s vision is that African research increasingly contributes to real world constructive change and its impact goal is a more equitable role for African journals within the global research publishing landscape. 

AJOL is a critical open content host and journal index for the African continent and has the potential to influence the global effort towards Open Science.</narrative>
  </description>
